  "output": "**No — it was refused on the first attempt.** Exact reason, verbatim:\n\n```\nRefusing to overwrite /workspace/project/inventory.txt: it changed on disk after you read it. Another agent is working in this directory. Read the file again, re-apply your change to the current content, then write. If you only need to change part of it, prefer edit_file — it re-reads the file itself and cannot clobber a concurrent edit.\n```\n\nThe `overwrite_read_confirm` flag didn't override it, which is worth knowing: that flag waives the *\"not fully read this session\"* guard, not the *\"changed on disk since the read\"* guard. They're separate checks.\n\nI then read the file rather than blindly retrying. Contents were:\n\n```\napples=3\nbananas=6\ncherries=7\ndates=9\n```\n\nThat's exactly the state from my previous edit — no other agent had actually altered it. The guard tripped because my `edit_file` changed the file *after* the session's last full read, so the tracked snapshot went stale by its own accounting. A false positive on \"another agent,\" in other words.\n\nWith a fresh read in hand, the second attempt succeeded: 17 bytes (`kiwis=1\\nlemons=2\\n`), two lines. If the file is touched by anything else before you ask for another blind overwrite, expect that same refusal message again — the flag won't get you past it.",
